        "original_id": "12f9d1fa-06bd-5fd5-96f5-6993dcef0413",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Stuart\n- Roles: Sir Joseph Porter, K.C.B.; Ko-Ko; Reginald Bunthorne\n- Works: H.M.S. Pinafore; The Mikado; Patience\n- Concepts: patter roles; patter song\n\nFacts:\n- James Stuart became a specialist in the patter roles in Gilbert and Sullivan operas.\n- James Stuart performed patter roles including Sir Joseph Porter, K.C.B. in H.M.S. Pinafore, Ko-Ko in The Mikado, and Reginald Bunthorne in Patience.\n- A patter song is characterized by a moderately fast to very fast tempo.\n- A patter song uses a rapid succession of rhythmic patterns in which each syllable of text corresponds to one note.",
